cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this book, its companion code, Shiny apps, or quiz bank,
  please cite it as below. Replace the placeholder repository URL
  once this project is published to its permanent GitHub location.
title: "R for Health Economics and Outcomes Research (HEOR) and Health Technology Assessment (HTA)"
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: Karunakaran
    given-names: Aswath
    name-particle: Dr
abstract: >-
  A 35-chapter technical book teaching R for health economics and
  outcomes research (HEOR) and health technology assessment (HTA),
  covering data management, statistical methods (survival analysis,
  meta-analysis, network meta-analysis, population-adjusted indirect
  comparisons, Bayesian methods, real-world evidence and causal
  inference, regression modelling), decision-analytic modelling
  (decision trees, Markov cohort models, partitioned survival models,
  microsimulation, discrete event simulation, budget impact analysis),
  uncertainty/value-of-information/validation, reproducible reporting
  and Shiny deployment, HTA agency practice, and six end-to-end worked
  case studies. Includes a companion GitHub repository with runnable
  R code for every chapter, interactive Shiny apps, a 661-question
  quiz bank, and example data sets.
keywords:
  - health economics
  - health technology assessment
  - HEOR
  - HTA
  - R
  - cost-effectiveness analysis
  - decision modelling
  - survival analysis
  - pharmacoeconomics
license-url: "https://github.com/askwith13/R_for_HEOR_and_HTA/blob/main/LICENSE"
